<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brades</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brades is a village in the north of Montserrat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> that has served as the island's de facto capital since the eruptions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soufriere-hills">Soufrière Hills volcano</a> destroyed the official capital, Plymouth, in 1997. Government offices moved there after the southern part of the island was declared an exclusion zone, and a new town at nearby Little Bay is planned as the permanent capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brades.jpg" alt="Brades" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Mergili · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brades_administration_2019.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
